# milestone_0021 PR3b part 1: the V4 agent primary attachment DATA, its signed attach/detach packets, the
# shared controller-signed action authorization, and the release/pane-io PORT contracts
# (.spipe/simple_orchestrator/continuation_20261116/milestone_0021_agent_owner_v4/DESIGN.md sections 13, 14,
# 14A, 14B, 14C; 14C wins over 14B wins over 14A wins over 14 wins over 13). SOURCE_AUTHORED / NOT_RUN.
#
# This module never imports the agent owner (the agent imports it). Agent-level transitions (begin_stop, the
# after-release hook, the step order, pane io, the lease accessor) live in host_linux_service_agent_v4.spl.
#
# The step machine calls a release PORT `fn(HostAgentAttachmentPortCallV4) -> HostAgentAttachmentReleaseStepV4`
# for every attachment sub-step that touches native state (OP open, RP expire, FL classification, RV/CL/ST
# resume). The machine itself does d1 REVOKE, the deadlines, the refusal and non-advancing counters, RB, the
# RT/RF writes and the hook. PR3b part 2 binds the production port (`host_agent_attachment_release_step_v4`:
# U', S, F/B, RP, geometry drain) and the production pane io port (`host_agent_pane_io_port_v4`).
# milestone_0023 part B binds the attach effects
# (`host_agent_attachment_open_step_v4`: helper prepare, then helper begin + open core + adoption).
